# User-suggestion GitHub issues

Issues labeled **`user-suggestion`** come from the in-app Suggestions product
(Edge `suggestion-github-issue`). They are **not** engineer-authored specs.

## Before coding

1. **Fetch Export JSON** — open the issue’s **Export JSON** link (footer). That
   payload is the source of truth: title, description, category, status, votes,
   author, and the full comment thread. Do not work from the GitHub body alone;
   it is a snapshot and may omit later in-app comments.
2. **Prioritize SuperAdmin comments** — in export JSON, any comment (or author)
   with `author.isSuperAdmin: true` is product direction. Treat those as
   authoritative clarification of intent, constraints, and preferred shape.
   When SuperAdmin guidance conflicts with the submitter’s literal wording,
   follow SuperAdmin and note the delta in the issue thread.
3. **Read community comments** — peer comments and `voteCount` are signals of
   shared pain, not a mandate to ship the proposed UI/API as written.

```bash
# Prefer the Export JSON URL from the issue body (app host injects anon key):
curl -sS "https://<app-host>/api/suggestion-export?id=<uuid>"
# Or: gh issue view <n> --json body,labels,comments
```

## Interpret, don’t copy-paste

End-user submissions often misuse product terms, propose incomplete logic, or
conflate problem and solution. **Respect the spirit** (job-to-be-done, pain,
desired outcome); **do not** implement a bad literal design.

Before implementing, think through:

| Lens | Ask |
| ---- | --- |
| **Problem vs solution** | What failure mode or unmet need is underneath the ask? |
| **Yowl fit** | Does it serve short-lived group chat (trips/conferences)? Prefer Slack-baseline utility over novelty. See [`docs/ux.md`](../docs/ux.md). |
| **Existing surface** | Can this be a small extension of room chat, invite, members, composer, or notifications — not a new IA island? |
| **Consent & privacy** | Joining is explicit; no silent membership or surprise side effects. Phone-identity users deserve careful defaults. |
| **Mobile / PWA first** | Thumb reach, keyboard, safe areas, offline shell — desktop-only solutions fail the product. |
| **Honesty of states** | Loading / empty / error / destructive confirm — never blank. Match [ux-standards](ux-standards.mdc). |
| **Scope** | Smallest change that delivers the outcome. Defer adjacent “while we’re here” features. |
| **Duplicates** | Search open/`user-suggestion` issues and the codebase before adding parallel features. |

## Propose alterations in the issue thread

If the best approach differs from the submitter’s ask (rename, narrower MVP,
different interaction, “won’t do / already exists”), **comment on the GitHub
issue before or with the PR** (`gh issue comment`). Cover:

1. **Understood need** — one sentence in plain language
2. **Proposed approach** — what you will (or won’t) build and why
3. **Trade-offs** — what you are consciously dropping
4. **Open questions** — only true product ambiguities (user gates); otherwise decide and document

Do not silently ship a reinterpretation. SuperAdmin can correct course on the
thread or in-app.

## Guardrails while building

- User-facing copy says **Yowl**, never Quacker; sentence case; no developer jargon in errors
- Membership-scoped data; RLS + Edge for anything privileged (UI gates are UX only)
- Update Playwright / Maestro selectors in the same change when labels/`aria-label`s change
- Prefer patterns already in the app (`MorphingPopover`, `QuickModal`, `@@ui`, optimistic toggles)
- After ship: leave the issue/PR linked; do not claim “done” in-app status unless a SuperAdmin workflow owns that update

## Anti-patterns

- Implementing the suggestion title as a feature name without checking Export JSON / SuperAdmin comments
- Treating the GitHub issue body as complete after in-app discussion continued
- Shipping a kitchen-sink settings page or dashboard chrome for a one-tap chat need
- Asking the human owner to “decide the UX” when the north star and SuperAdmin notes already constrain the answer
